+++ b/docs/code/compat/alpha_movie.md
@@ -0,0 +1,39 @@
+# AlphaMovie: pull-driven AJPM animation
+
+`Plugins.link("AlphaMovie.dll")` installs the reference `AlphaMovie` class.
+The game's script wrapper owns animation timing and may create its own
+`alphamovie_object`; the native does not synthesize that game-owned object.
+
+`AlphaMovieSource` opens independent `AlphaMovieSession: Send` values on the
+VM thread. The composition root reads mounted storage and uses the L1
+`media::alpha_movie` codec. L3 never links a codec or sends a storage pointer,
+VM context or scene handle to the decoder worker.
+
+The native owns one prefetch worker per playing instance. The worker owns
+its session and decodes outside queue locks. Ready frames are bounded by
+`preloadSamples` (default 5, accepted range 1..=30) and a 128 MiB RGBA budget;
+at most one decoded frame may wait outside that queue. The app separately
+limits each expanded frame to 64 MiB. Memory policy reports an oversized
+frame rather than dropping it. Compressed input and codec working planes
+are additional allocations.
+
+`showNextImage(layer)` is a nonblocking pull. A starved queue retains the
+last displayed frame; there is no second native clock. A ready rectangle
+replaces the layer's pixels and combines its origin with the script position.
+Padded and empty rectangles are valid. Decoder position and displayed frame
+are distinct reference properties.
+
+Generation checks discard results from superseded seeks, opens or clears.
+The worker reports a next-file request to the VM, where the source factory
+opens the next session; only the owned session crosses back to the worker.
+Stop and destruction wake and join outside queue locks. A currently executing
+decode must return before joining can complete. Errors are typed and surface
+through native calls; a missing queued next file ends the stream as the
+reference does. EOF does not clear the reference play flag or implicitly
+restart the worker; explicit play restarts from the beginning.
+
+The reference is `cpp/plugins/AlphaMovie.cpp`, including the pre-decode EOF
+check, final-index seek behavior, queue starvation, stop, clear and chained
+movies. Tests use gated decoder sessions and condition-variable progress
+rather than assuming synchronous prefetch. Pixel tests separately cover AJPM
+separate-zlib and block-alpha streams.
