+the demuxed stream's packet time base. The codec removes encoder priming;
+neither reads nor seeks remove it again. The reported total frames come from
+container timing at the decoded rate. An unknown duration remains `None`
+until playback reaches the end. Raw PCM may include end padding beyond this
+nominal length; playback clips at the container length selected by the host.
+
+A seek transactionally reopens the same compressed bytes, then discards to
+the target frame on subsequent reads. It is sample accurate but linear in
+the target distance. A failed reopen or overflowing sample position leaves
+the existing stream usable. A decode error following a partial read is
+reported on the next call, so returned PCM is preserved. Accepted streams
+report later decode failures instead of silently switching backends.
